WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.350 --> 00:00:02.970
- [Presenter] This is
the Ukrainian village

00:00:02.970 --> 00:00:06.390
of Nyzhni Sirohozy in the
occupied Kherson region

00:00:06.390 --> 00:00:10.830
in October, 2022, and in March, 2023.

00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:12.960
The new lines in the fields are rows

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:15.870
of Russian fortifications
built in anticipation

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:18.780
of a counter-offensive by Ukraine.

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:20.790
While Kyiv has been training its troops

00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:22.890
to use Western weapons,

00:00:22.890 --> 00:00:24.090
Russia has been building

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:26.820
some of the most extensive
defensive lines seen

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:28.980
anywhere in the world in decades,

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:31.106
according to Western intelligence.

00:00:31.106 --> 00:00:35.189
(speaking in a foreign language)

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:39.570
A military analyst who spoke
to the "Wall Street Journal"

00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:41.820
say they're skeptical of the effectiveness

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:43.890
of these defenses.

00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:46.950
The "Journal" analyzed
satellite images and videos

00:00:46.950 --> 00:00:50.490
from Russian media to understand
what Moscow's preparations

00:00:50.490 --> 00:00:51.993
could mean for Ukraine.

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:55.320
Since the start of the invasion,

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:58.680
Russia has been digging
along the 900-mile front line

00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:00.900
and even on its own territory.

00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:03.630
Much of the work is focused
on the occupied areas

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:06.420
of the Zaporizhzhia and Kherson regions,

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:10.260
according to data collected
by a satellite image analyst.

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:14.040
British intelligence say
Russia has built 75 miles

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:16.980
of defensive lines in Zaporizhzhia.

00:01:16.980 --> 00:01:18.720
This hints at where Russia expects

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:20.640
to be attacked by Ukraine,

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:22.170
and many Western analysts agree

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:24.510
that these territories
could be the main targets

00:01:24.510 --> 00:01:26.253
of Ukraine's counteroffensive.

00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:30.240
So here's what Russia has been building.

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:33.720
The first layer of defense
shown in many satellite images

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:35.970
is the anti-tank ditch.

00:01:35.970 --> 00:01:39.510
The obstacle is meant to be
too wide for a tank to cross,

00:01:39.510 --> 00:01:42.420
restricting an enemy's
ability to maneuver,

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:44.580
and funnel their forces into areas

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:47.370
that make them more vulnerable to attack.

00:01:47.370 --> 00:01:51.240
Next are rows of concrete
blocks called dragon's teeth.

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:53.460
They form a barrier
that makes it difficult

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:55.800
for heavy vehicles to pass through.

00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:57.990
And the third line is a trench.

00:01:57.990 --> 00:02:00.630
This is the most common
type of defensive work

00:02:00.630 --> 00:02:02.670
and the easiest to construct.

00:02:02.670 --> 00:02:05.280
Russian forces dug many
trenches along roads,

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:09.540
junctions and bridges, and
even on the beaches of Crimea.

00:02:09.540 --> 00:02:13.080
Most of them were built at
a zigzag or angular pattern.

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:15.570
This limit the sight lines for the enemy

00:02:15.570 --> 00:02:17.010
and offers additional protection

00:02:17.010 --> 00:02:19.443
from shell fragments coming from the side.

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:24.480
And Ukrainian forces are
likely to face further traps.

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:26.460
Military analysts believe landmines

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:29.163
have also been hidden
between defensive lines.

00:02:30.090 --> 00:02:33.390
Ukraine's and Russia's ministries
of defense didn't respond

00:02:33.390 --> 00:02:35.670
to our request for comments
on the significance

00:02:35.670 --> 00:02:37.923
of Moscow's fortification efforts.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:42.150
Some military experts
say these defense systems

00:02:42.150 --> 00:02:45.900
don't necessarily pose a major
threat to the Ukrainians.

00:02:45.900 --> 00:02:48.600
They say whether the
fortifications are effective

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:52.410
would depend on the number of
Russian troops defending them,

00:02:52.410 --> 00:02:54.480
and if Ukraine attacks defensive lines

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:56.580
that aren't sufficiently protected,

00:02:56.580 --> 00:02:59.550
the Ukrainians will be able
to bypass the obstacles

00:02:59.550 --> 00:03:02.910
with Western Challenger
and Leopard battle tanks.

00:03:02.910 --> 00:03:04.950
Experts say that in the end,

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:07.980
intelligence on the position
of Russian troops will be key

00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:10.110
to Ukraine's counteroffensive,

00:03:10.110 --> 00:03:12.690
and whether they can force
Russia to concentrate troops

00:03:12.690 --> 00:03:16.188
in the wrong place and leave
defensive lines exposed.

00:03:16.188 --> 00:03:18.771
(guns banging)

